  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Delér took control of the family painting company in the early 1990s as its fifth-generation proprietor. Accounts of the business describe growth from six employees and modest turnover to more than one hundred staff. He then combined its window-renovation activity with that of another established contractor, creating Bruske Delér to serve institutional and private property owners around Stockholm.\n\nA move to southern Spain opened a different chapter. Delér co-founded Homerun Brokers in Marbella, bringing his public profile and brand reach to luxury residential sales before leaving the company. He has also held interests in hospitality and clothing, supported school-building projects in Colombia and moved into the Cypriot solar sector. His Instagram and YouTube channels document renovation, business and family projects for a sizeable audience.",
    "html": "<p>Delér took control of the family painting company in the early 1990s as its fifth-generation proprietor. Accounts of the business describe growth from six employees and modest turnover to more than one hundred staff. He then combined its window-renovation activity with that of another established contractor, creating Bruske Delér to serve institutional and private property owners around Stockholm.</p>\r\n<p>A move to southern Spain opened a different chapter. Delér co-founded Homerun Brokers in Marbella, bringing his public profile and brand reach to luxury residential sales before leaving the company. He has also held interests in hospitality and clothing, supported school-building projects in Colombia and moved into the Cypriot solar sector. His Instagram and YouTube channels document renovation, business and family projects for a sizeable audience.</p>\r\n",
